1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,200
Hi everybody, this is the Triple P, Patricia Pie podcast.

2
00:00:08,200 --> 00:00:16,560
It has taken me many, many moons, my friends, to get, it's always hard, to get Patricia into

3
00:00:16,560 --> 00:00:19,600
the studio here at the cottage.

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:25,640
Many people have requested, we play more of her songs, listen to more of her story, and

5
00:00:25,640 --> 00:00:33,640
this is the only show where your biggest fan gets to ask you questions and play your music.

6
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:34,640
And that's you?

7
00:00:34,640 --> 00:00:35,640
That's me.

8
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:36,640
Oh, that's so sweet.

9
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:38,640
Well, thank you for having me, Mr. Curry.

10
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:39,640
Yes.

11
00:00:39,640 --> 00:00:44,640
And you know why I never want to do this, because I don't like to look back.

12
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:45,640
You know that.

13
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:46,640
Yeah, but...

14
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:50,640
You never hear me talk about it or...

15
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:51,640
No, never ever.

16
00:00:51,640 --> 00:00:52,640
No, I know.

17
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:53,640
So how come...

18
00:00:53,640 --> 00:00:54,640
Always look ahead.

19
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:56,640
So let's start right now.

20
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:59,640
Why did you decide to do the podcast?

21
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,640
Because you're asking me.

22
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:02,640
I know.

23
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,640
Knife on the throat.

24
00:01:04,640 --> 00:01:07,640
That's all it took, is someone to ask you?

25
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:08,640
That's all?

26
00:01:08,640 --> 00:01:10,640
And you helped me in the kitchen?

27
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:11,640
Oh, okay.

28
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:12,640
You did.

29
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:13,640
I noticed.

30
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:16,640
So can I start off with one of my favorite songs that you've done?

31
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,640
Because, you know what?

32
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:22,640
We have like four CDs, which is probably 5% of all the music you've made.

33
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:23,640
Yes.

34
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:24,640
It's just ridiculous.

35
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:25,640
Yeah.

36
00:01:25,640 --> 00:01:27,640
How come you didn't look after your shit, man?

37
00:01:27,640 --> 00:01:29,640
You should have at least kept the CDs.

38
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:31,640
See, that's why you're always yelling at me.

39
00:01:31,640 --> 00:01:32,640
No, no, no.

40
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:35,640
Because I made a lot of records.

41
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,640
How many do you make?

42
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:38,640
What's a lot?

43
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:39,640
What's a lot?

44
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:43,640
I think 75 to 100 records.

45
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,640
Albums and CDs?

46
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:46,640
No.

47
00:01:46,640 --> 00:01:50,640
And then say about 30 to 40 albums.

48
00:01:50,640 --> 00:01:51,640
No shit.

49
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:53,640
So you have hundreds of songs?

50
00:01:53,640 --> 00:01:54,640
Yes.

51
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:56,640
Maybe even like a thousand?

52
00:01:56,640 --> 00:02:01,640
Sometimes people play me something and I don't even know it's me or I know the song.

53
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:02,640
I don't even know the song.

54
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:03,640
I know.

55
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:05,640
It's happened to me a couple of times on the hit test.

56
00:02:05,640 --> 00:02:06,640
It's scary.

57
00:02:06,640 --> 00:02:13,640
If you meet people who know the lyrics or sing along and I think, shit, that's strange.

58
00:02:13,640 --> 00:02:18,640
And I will tell you later what happens in my dreams because of this.

59
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:20,640
Is that the one with the hookers?

60
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:22,640
No.

61
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:23,640
Okay.

62
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:29,640
I'm going to start off with, this is the genre I like that you do best.

63
00:02:29,640 --> 00:02:37,640
Yeah, this is actually, I started with this sort of music because my daddy is a band leader.

64
00:02:38,750 --> 00:06:08,750
[ Music ]

65
00:06:14,640 --> 00:06:17,640
You've got a little Ella there at the end.

66
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:19,640
Excuse me, put the mic in front of your mouth.

67
00:06:19,640 --> 00:06:21,640
Ella was my favorite.

68
00:06:21,640 --> 00:06:26,640
So when I started to sing these sort of songs, I was 15 years old.

69
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:34,640
15, and when I was 17, I went to the nightclub where my dad's band played.

70
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:39,640
And in the weekend, I did some songs in the nightclub.

71
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,640
And how old were you, 15?

72
00:06:43,640 --> 00:06:44,640
I was 17 then.

73
00:06:44,640 --> 00:06:49,640
Actually too young, because you're not allowed in the nightclub.

74
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,640
You weren't allowed to work officially?

75
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:52,640
No, no, no, no.

76
00:06:52,640 --> 00:06:56,640
So that was recorded in, I think, 2001?

77
00:06:56,640 --> 00:07:00,640
Yeah, I did it again with my dad's band.

78
00:07:00,640 --> 00:07:04,640
My dad is now, what is he, 78?

79
00:07:04,640 --> 00:07:06,640
No, he's 79.

80
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:09,640
In 1978, he will be 79 this year.

81
00:07:09,640 --> 00:07:14,640
And the band that you just heard, they're all grandfathers.

82
00:07:14,640 --> 00:07:15,640
They're all his friends.

83
00:07:15,640 --> 00:07:17,640
Those guys are like half dead, I remember that.

84
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:20,640
This is sort of a hobby band, and they still make beautiful music.

85
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:24,640
So you see that it doesn't matter how old you are,

86
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:27,640
you can always play music and make music and it's lovely.

87
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:32,640
So that's why I wanted to record it, because it's wonderful.

88
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:33,640
78, maybe.

89
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:36,640
There was even one guy, 80.

90
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:39,640
Was that the guy that couldn't show up one day for recording,

91
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:42,640
because they had...

92
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,640
Yeah, how is that in English?

93
00:07:44,640 --> 00:07:45,640
Dottere.

94
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,640
What is the word?

95
00:07:47,640 --> 00:07:50,640
They had to go to the hospital to let his veins,

96
00:07:50,640 --> 00:07:52,640
like they cleaned the veins.

97
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:53,640
I can't think of the word.

98
00:07:53,640 --> 00:07:54,640
Drew's heart, I don't know.

99
00:07:54,640 --> 00:07:56,640
Dutch is Dottere.

100
00:07:56,640 --> 00:07:58,640
Yeah, pump up the volume.

101
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:00,640
Yeah, that was good though.

102
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,640
They're so sweet if you see guys playing.

103
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:08,640
And that was on a Special Collector's Edition EP.

104
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:14,640
Actually, it's a very special CD, because it only has four songs on it.

105
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:16,640
Hold on, I have it here in iTunes.

106
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:21,640
We recorded it actually, especially for friends and family,

107
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:23,640
and just give it away to them.

108
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:26,640
And a little known fact is that on the CD,

109
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:31,640
the title for Misty and a Foggy Day have been reversed.

110
00:08:31,640 --> 00:08:33,640
Yes, that was wrong.

111
00:08:33,640 --> 00:08:37,640
Like 1500 CDs were the wrong track titles.

112
00:08:37,640 --> 00:08:38,640
Exactly, yeah.

113
00:08:38,640 --> 00:08:40,640
I love that though, I love it.

114
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:44,640
And that makes me think of the time you sang with Tony Bennett.

115
00:08:44,640 --> 00:08:46,640
I don't have that recording unfortunate.

116
00:08:46,640 --> 00:08:47,640
That was only on CD.

117
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,640
No, we have it on tape, on videotape.

118
00:08:49,640 --> 00:08:50,640
Your parents have that?

119
00:08:50,640 --> 00:08:51,640
No, we have it.

120
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:52,640
We have it here?

121
00:08:52,640 --> 00:08:53,640
We have it too.

122
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:54,640
What, on VHS or something?

123
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:56,640
Probably, yeah, yeah.

124
00:08:56,640 --> 00:09:02,640
And it was a very famous program in Holland that we had with Pim Jakobs,

125
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:05,640
one of the best jazz musicians.

126
00:09:05,640 --> 00:09:07,640
Yeah, lots of people know Pim Jakobs and jazz.

127
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:12,640
Yeah, and Rochie van Otlo, one of the, what is it?

128
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:13,640
Conductor.

129
00:09:13,640 --> 00:09:16,640
Conductors of beautiful big band.

130
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:18,640
Tony Bennett was in the show that evening.

131
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:24,640
And I had to sing a duet with him, I remember.

132
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:27,640
And the song that they chose, I didn't like.

133
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:29,640
Well, you did two songs, didn't you do two songs?

134
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:33,640
Yeah, I did two songs myself and I had to sing a duet with Tony Bennett.

135
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:34,640
Yeah.

136
00:09:34,640 --> 00:09:36,640
And I hated that song.

137
00:09:36,640 --> 00:09:38,640
And didn't you tell him that?

138
00:09:38,640 --> 00:09:40,640
Yes, I said, I'm not going to sing.

139
00:09:40,640 --> 00:09:42,640
Even if it's with you, I'm not going to sing it.

140
00:09:42,640 --> 00:09:43,640
I hate it.

141
00:09:43,640 --> 00:09:44,640
You said that to Tony Bennett?

142
00:09:44,640 --> 00:09:45,640
Yeah.

143
00:09:45,640 --> 00:09:46,640
And what did you say?

144
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:47,640
Yo.

145
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:49,640
I said, no, I don't like it.

146
00:09:49,640 --> 00:09:50,640
And so we skipped it.

147
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:51,640
We didn't do it.

148
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:52,640
What song did you wind up doing?

149
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:53,640
No, we did.

150
00:09:53,640 --> 00:09:57,640
At the end, we all sang a sort of a song together.

151
00:09:57,640 --> 00:10:00,640
So you actually, you didn't really sing a full duet with Tony Bennett

152
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:01,640
because you didn't like the song?

153
00:10:01,640 --> 00:10:02,640
No.

154
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:03,640
You don't even remember what song it was?

155
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:04,640
But he made a beautiful drawing for me.

156
00:10:04,640 --> 00:10:05,640
That's true.

157
00:10:05,640 --> 00:10:06,640
And I still have it.

158
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,640
You still have that?

159
00:10:07,640 --> 00:10:08,640
Yeah.

160
00:10:08,640 --> 00:10:10,640
He's quite a painter and a very nice man.

161
00:10:10,640 --> 00:10:13,640
And he said to me, I heard that you are actually a rock singer.

162
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:16,640
He said, but don't ever do that with your voice.

163
00:10:16,640 --> 00:10:17,640
This is what you should do.

164
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:18,640
Yeah.

165
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:19,640
I agree.

166
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:20,640
Fuckin' A. Tony's right.

167
00:10:20,640 --> 00:10:22,640
But this music is wonderful.

168
00:10:22,640 --> 00:10:23,640
You can always sing it.

169
00:10:23,640 --> 00:10:26,640
You can always, even, it doesn't matter how old you are.

170
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:29,640
I hope this music will always stay.

171
00:10:29,640 --> 00:10:31,640
Even with Frank Sinatra gone.

172
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:32,640
Don't you think so?

173
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:33,640
Oh yeah.

174
00:10:33,640 --> 00:10:34,640
And we really miss him.

175
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:35,640
Don't we miss him?

176
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:36,640
Absolutely.

177
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:37,640
Fuckin' Lutely.

178
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:40,640
Remember we saw him, one of his last shows at the Meadowlands in New Jersey?

179
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:41,640
We did.

180
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:42,640
Aren't we lucky?

181
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:43,640
And it was canceled because he felt ill.

182
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:44,640
And we thought, oh shit, man.

183
00:10:44,640 --> 00:10:45,640
I was gonna fucking die.

184
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:47,640
He was really bad at that time.

185
00:10:47,640 --> 00:10:49,640
He was on the ropes.

186
00:10:49,640 --> 00:10:50,640
I've seen him twice.

187
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:51,640
I'm so happy.

188
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:52,640
Yeah.

189
00:10:52,640 --> 00:10:56,640
I wish I'd seen the one at Madison Square Garden that they did the live recording.

190
00:10:56,640 --> 00:10:58,640
We've seen the one with Liza Minnelli.

191
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:00,640
We saw the one with Liza Minnelli.

192
00:11:00,640 --> 00:11:01,640
Yeah.

193
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:02,640
Yeah.

194
00:11:02,640 --> 00:11:03,640
That's right.

195
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:04,640
Yeah.

196
00:11:04,640 --> 00:11:05,640
She was pretty sober.

197
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:06,640
Yeah.

198
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:07,640
She was pretty good actually.

199
00:11:07,640 --> 00:11:08,640
Yeah.

200
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:09,640
But not anymore.

201
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:11,640
Now she's, the voice you got, ah, ah, ah, ah.

202
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:13,640
When they do that, you know, it's screwed.

203
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,640
It's all over.

204
00:11:14,640 --> 00:11:15,640
It's screwed.

205
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:16,640
Yeah.

206
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:22,640
So what most people don't know is that you don't sing.

207
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:23,640
What?

208
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:24,640
I mean, well, you don't sing.

209
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:25,640
You don't sing around the house.

210
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:26,640
No.

211
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:27,640
I mean, once in a while maybe.

212
00:11:27,640 --> 00:11:28,640
No.

213
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:29,640
I only sing for money.

214
00:11:29,640 --> 00:11:30,640
Exactly.

215
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:33,640
Now, I think you should explain this because it's very hard for people to understand,

216
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:34,640
even for me actually.

217
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:37,640
I mean, if I could sing like you, I would be all over the place.

218
00:11:37,640 --> 00:11:39,640
I'd be like, yo.

219
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:42,640
Well, there are all sorts of performances.

220
00:11:42,640 --> 00:11:44,640
Performers, I think.

221
00:11:44,640 --> 00:11:45,640
Mm-hmm.

222
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:56,640
And because my dad is a musician that had to work really hard to take care of his family.

223
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:57,640
Mm-hmm.

224
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:00,640
And so I didn't know what to become and what to do.

225
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:02,640
And I thought, oh, I'm going to be a singer then.

226
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:03,640
Yeah.

227
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:08,640
So because we all got something of music in our bodies.

228
00:12:08,640 --> 00:12:10,640
And so I started to sing.

229
00:12:10,640 --> 00:12:18,640
But in these days, you, especially in clubs and in hotels and everything,

230
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:23,640
Germany and Belgium and Holland, that was for the money.

231
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,640
And that's how I started.

232
00:12:25,640 --> 00:12:26,640
And then when suddenly somebody…

233
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:27,640
It was just a job.

234
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:28,640
Yeah, it was a job.

235
00:12:28,640 --> 00:12:29,640
It was just my job.

236
00:12:29,640 --> 00:12:31,640
I didn't know what to do, what kind of job.

237
00:12:31,640 --> 00:12:33,640
I thought, okay, then I'll do it.

238
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,640
But didn't you like it too?

239
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:35,640
I loved it.

240
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:37,640
There were moments that I really enjoyed it.

241
00:12:37,640 --> 00:12:39,640
But there were a lot of moments I hated it.

242
00:12:39,640 --> 00:12:40,640
Okay.

243
00:12:40,640 --> 00:12:42,640
Let's start with the enjoying moments.

244
00:12:42,640 --> 00:12:48,640
Well, you know, if you have wonderful audience and people are really swinging along

245
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:52,640
and looking at you like, wow, you know, there was a great evening

246
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:54,640
because we enjoyed the music so much.

247
00:12:54,640 --> 00:12:58,640
But you had also evenings that people were very drunk,

248
00:12:58,640 --> 00:13:01,640
didn't hear anything, were talking really loud.

249
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:03,640
And that's horrible.

250
00:13:03,640 --> 00:13:06,640
Then sound comes out of your mouth.

251
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:07,640
But what do you like more?

252
00:13:07,640 --> 00:13:10,640
Do you like performing, recording, writing?

253
00:13:10,640 --> 00:13:14,640
What I always liked was recording.

254
00:13:14,640 --> 00:13:16,640
Right, that makes sense.

255
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,640
So coming up with ideas, doing backups.

256
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,640
And I love that.

257
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:25,640
Although they say I'm a very good performer.

258
00:13:25,640 --> 00:13:27,640
I can really…

259
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,640
How do you say that?

260
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,640
You can rock the house, baby.

261
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:35,640
Put on a show.

262
00:13:36,640 --> 00:13:39,640
I'm trying to think what we should play next.

263
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:42,640
I mean, we have four CDs, hold on.

264
00:13:42,640 --> 00:13:46,640
Well, if we have to go through the whole story, it takes very long.

265
00:13:46,640 --> 00:13:47,640
Oh, no, we'll never be able to do that.

266
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:49,640
Well, maybe we'll do it in parts.

267
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,640
Yeah, we'll do another one another time.

268
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:52,640
But we need more music.

